    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="meta">Updated 4 Oct 2026 · Operator: OndysLab s.r.o., hello@trypup.life</p>

    <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
    <p>By downloading and using the Trypup app you agree to these terms. If you disagree, do not use the app. The contract for use of the app is concluded with the operator, OndysLab s.r.o.</p>

    <h2>2. Service description</h2>
    <p>Trypup is an <strong>educational simulator</strong> of dog care for education and entertainment. It is <strong>not a substitute</strong> for veterinary, training or other professional care of a real animal. In-app information (costs, vaccinations, articles) is indicative.</p>

    <h2>3. User age</h2>
    <p>The app is intended for users <strong>aged 13 and over</strong> (App Store and Google Play rating). Users <strong>under 16</strong> use it <strong>with the consent of a parent or legal guardian</strong>; the app does not offer them purchases and does not collect analytics about them (see the Privacy Policy). A user under 16 creates an account only with a parent's consent; a parent may request its deletion at any time.</p>

    <h2>4. No veterinary advice</h2>
    <p>Health and cost content is general and educational. For a real dog, always follow the advice of a licensed veterinarian.</p>

    <h2>5. Account and shared care</h2>
    <p>An account is optional — it backs up your saved progress and enables <strong>shared care</strong> of a dog with your family. You are responsible for your credentials and for actions taken under your account. The dog's owner can add members with an invite code and remove them at any time; a member sees the dog's state, completed tasks and the display names of other members, and can leave at any time. We may end sharing if it is abused. You can delete your account directly in the app (Profile → Account → Delete account) or via the <a href="/en/delete-account/">Delete account</a> page.</p>

    <h2>6. Premium, payments and the seller</h2>
    <p>The app offers optional paid features (Premium subscription and individual breeds). These purchases are sold and billed by the operator of the relevant store — <strong>Apple (App Store)</strong> or <strong>Google (Google Play)</strong> — who acts as the seller toward you. Prices are shown in the store including all taxes; OndysLab s.r.o. is not a VAT payer, and the store handles tax and the tax receipt. Subscriptions renew automatically at the displayed price until you cancel them in the subscription settings of the App Store or Google Play — at least 24 hours before the end of the current period. Previously purchased features can be restored on a new device with the “Restore purchases” button in the app.</p>

    <h2>7. Withdrawal and refunds</h2>
    <p>Because the seller is Apple or Google, withdrawal from a purchase and refunds are governed by the rules of the relevant store. You request a refund in the App Store (reportaproblem.apple.com) or in Google Play. Please note that for digital content supplied online, the right of withdrawal ceases under Section 1837(l) of the Czech Civil Code once performance has begun with your prior express consent and acknowledgement that you lose that right.</p>

    <h2>8. Defects and complaints for digital content</h2>
    <p>We strive to keep the digital content conforming to its description and functional, and we provide updates necessary to maintain it. As a consumer you have the statutory rights arising from defective performance under the Czech Civil Code. Report a defect or problem to <a href="mailto:hello@trypup.life">hello@trypup.life</a>; refunds are handled by the store where you made the purchase.</p>

    <h2>9. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You must not misuse the app, spoof GPS data, decompile it, circumvent its protective mechanisms or break applicable law. Shared-care invite codes are meant only for the people you really share the dog with — do not publish them.</p>

    <h2>10. Licence and content</h2>
    <p>The app, its texts, icons, graphics and educational articles are protected by the operator's copyright. We grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable licence for personal, non-commercial use of the app. Data you enter into the app (such as your dog's name) remain yours; you allow us to store them and show them to shared-care members to the extent needed for the service to work.</p>

    <h2>11. Availability and termination of the service</h2>
    <p>We develop the app continuously and may change it, temporarily limit it or discontinue it. We provide the cloud backup with professional care, but game progress has no monetary value and we do not compensate its loss due to an outage, deleting the app or discontinuing the service. We will give reasonable notice in the app before discontinuing the service.</p>

    <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>The app is provided "as is". To the maximum extent permitted by law we are not liable for indirect damages from its use. Nothing in these terms limits consumer rights under Czech and EU law.</p>

    <h2>13. Out-of-court dispute resolution</h2>
    <p>The <strong>Czech Trade Inspection Authority</strong> (Česká obchodní inspekce, Gorazdova 1969/24, 120 00 Prague 2, ID 000 20 869, <a href="https://adr.coi.cz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">adr.coi.cz</a>) is competent for out-of-court resolution of consumer disputes. Cross-border disputes are assisted by the <strong>European Consumer Centre Czech Republic</strong> (<a href="https://www.evropskyspotrebitel.cz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">evropskyspotrebitel.cz</a>). You can also send a complaint to <a href="mailto:hello@trypup.life">hello@trypup.life</a>; we will inform you of its handling by email. Consumer-protection supervision is exercised by the Czech Trade Inspection Authority and personal-data supervision by the Office for Personal Data Protection. We are not bound by any codes of conduct within the meaning of Section 1820(1)(n) of the Czech Civil Code.</p>

    <h2>14. Privacy</h2>
